      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALDEBARAN MISTIQUE (3) made a nice return at her latest appearance nine days ago, finishing 1.5 metres away in second over 1690m at Shepparton. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Tackles a similar assignment and she can continue the strong start to the campaign. OUR TINKA BELLE (2) faces the starter for the first time. By Majestic Son and hails from the Anthony Spiteri stable. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Placed in a recent trial and finds a nice race so anticipating a bright start to her career. MI BOW (6) did a good job to finish in the minor placings two runs back then things went sour last time when she broke and finished a long way back in ninth over 2240m at Melton. Only needs to get things right to be in the money. AMESKY (5) is worth some thought despite her last-start sixth over 1720m at Melton on July 18.",
